Create a Java program to demonstrate inheritance and method overriding using an employee management system.

Create a class Employee with:

instance variables: name (String) and salary (double)

a constructor to initialize these variables

a method getSalary() that returns the employee’s salary

Create a subclass Manager that extends Employee with:

an additional variable bonus (double)

a constructor that initializes name, salary, and bonus

override the getSalary() method to return salary + bonus

In the main() method:

create a Manager object

display the employee name and total salary

Concepts tested: inheritance, constructor chaining, method overriding, super keyword.